# JEREBU.EXE environment variables (added in Experiment 003, live evidence).
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development, or set the variables in
# your hosting provider's settings. NEVER commit real values: .env and .env.*
# files (except this one) are ignored by git.
#
# Both variables are read only by server code (src/lib/live/snapshots.ts) and
# are never sent to browsers. Do not rename them with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix:
# Next.js would then copy the value into the JavaScript sent to every visitor.
# Both are optional: the live evidence page works without either.

# NASA FIRMS MAP_KEY (free). Optional.
# Without it, the site reads NASA's openly downloadable "South East Asia,
# last 24 hours" VIIRS active fire files. With it, the site uses the documented
# FIRMS area API for the map window instead.
# A person requests one with an email address at:
#   https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# data.gov.sg API key. Optional, but data.gov.sg recommends a key for
# production use. Sent as the x-api-key header. Without a key, data.gov.sg's
# real-time APIs allow 6 calls per 10 seconds; with a key the limit is higher.
# How to request one:
#   https://guide.data.gov.sg/developer-guide/api-overview/how-to-request-an-api-key
DATA_GOV_SG_API_KEY=
